  "term": "automatic speaker recognition",
  "definition": "Automatic speaker recognition is the use of computer-based classification methods to identify who is speaking from features of their voice. In the source packet, its performance varied widely, and wearing a surgical mask appeared to reduce accuracy to some extent.",
