      "reasons": [
        "The first sentence’s description (computer-based classification to identify a speaker from voice features) is supported by the packet’s description of “classification analyses” for identifying individual speakers.",
        "The definition’s claim that “wearing a surgical mask appeared to reduce accuracy to some extent” is not directly supported as a reduction in accuracy. The packet reports highly-variable identification accuracies (40% to 89.2%), low performance in classifying mask vs no-mask (<50%), and an implication that masking “would impact” general performance, but it does not explicitly state that accuracy was reduced by wearing a mask.",
        "Because the accuracy-reduction wording is more specific than what the packet explicitly provides, the definition contains an unsupported substantive claim."
